 "sentences": [
  "It's crucial for collaborating on code and tracking changes.",
  "Always add the '@retry' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your functions.",
  "It's a requirement here, as it helps with error handling and makes your code more robust.",
  "Also, when you're working on a feature or a bug fix, create a new branch for it.",
  "Never work directly on the master branch.",
  "This is a standard Git workflow practice and ensures that your changes don't impact the main codebase until they're ready for merging.",
  "Document your code thoroughly using docstrings and comments.",
  "Finally, for now, don't hesitate to ask questions.",
  "The sooner you get up to speed, the better.",
  "We'll touch base regularly, but don't hesitate to seek me out if you need anything sooner.",
  "I want to ensure we're organized and prepared for each one.",
  "When you're coding, I want you to follow a specific convention for method and attribute names.",
  "Always start method names with 'b_'.",
  "For attribute names, include the string 'chx' somewhere in the name.",
  "Attention to detail is crucial, especially when we're representing ORBIT to clients and at industry events.",
  "Rado, I want you to start committing directly to the dev branch from now on.",
  "It's time to integrate your work with the rest of the team."
 ],
